From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: an extension may open its own popup

`action.openPopup()` opens the action's popup in the toolbar of a
browser window. A desk has no toolbar, so Chrome's function answers
"Could not find an active browser window." Phantom opens its popup
this way from every tray click: it clears its popup so the click
reaches `action.onClicked`, then sets it and calls `openPopup`.

- bindings: build DomicileExtensionPopupEvent and its init dictionary,
  the event behind DomicileHost.onextensionpopuprequested.

The function itself, the tray's message and the event are new files
under src/.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
